### Pattern 1: Worktree Deployment

**Setup Command**:
```bash
cd /home/lkonga/codes/psp-p2p
./scripts/validate-deployment.sh --type environment,directories --env staging
./scripts/local-sudo-runner/sudo-runner.sh --trunner \
  "./scripts/setup-worktree.sh {WORKTREE_NAME} \
    --setup-laravel \
    --source-worktree-type psp-p2p \
    --subdomain staging.{WORKTREE_NAME} \
    --source-branch develop \
    --psp-landing-worktree {LANDING_WORKTREE} \
    --psp-p2p-worktree {P2P_WORKTREE} \
    --ppp-worktree push-parser-panel"
```

**⚠️ CRITICAL**:
- `--subdomain` is **MANDATORY** for new worktree setup
- Subdomain MUST start with 'staging.' prefix
- Worktree name MUST match subdomain (minus 'staging.')
- `--source-branch` can be ANY existing branch (e.g., develop, main, feature/*) - script creates new branch from it

**Deploy Command**:
```bash
./scripts/local-sudo-runner/sudo-runner.sh --trunner \
  "./scripts/deploy-worktree.sh {WORKTREE_NAME} \\
    --source-worktree-type psp-p2p \\
    --domain trylatest.in \\
    --landing-url https://staging.{landing-subdomain}.trylatest.in \\
    --psp-url https://staging.{psp-subdomain}.trylatest.in \\
    --ppp-url https://staging.push-parser-panel.trylatest.in"
```

**Note**: Deploy command URLs should include 'staging.' prefix for local deployments.

**Note**: `--ppp-url` is **mandatory** for all deployments (worktree and main branch). Main branch deployments do NOT require `--subdomain` parameter (subdomain is derived from app-type).

> **Note**: Replace `{landing-subdomain}` and `{psp-subdomain}` with actual triad service subdomains. These can be any deployed service names (e.g., `psp-landing-preview-5`, `feature-x`, etc.).

**Repair Mode (Resetup)**:
```bash
# ⚠️ WARNING: --resetup is DESTRUCTIVE - see "CRITICAL WARNINGS" below
# Interactive mode (requires manual confirmation)
cd /home/lkonga/codes/psp-p2p
./scripts/local-sudo-runner/sudo-runner.sh --trunner \
  "./scripts/setup-worktree.sh {WORKTREE_NAME} \
    --resetup \
    --source-worktree-type psp-p2p \
    --psp-landing-worktree {LANDING_WORKTREE} \
    --psp-p2p-worktree {P2P_WORKTREE} \
    --ppp-worktree push-parser-panel"

# Automated mode (for testing - bypasses confirmation)
./scripts/local-sudo-runner/sudo-runner.sh --trunner \
  "./scripts/setup-worktree.sh {WORKTREE_NAME} \
    --resetup \
    --auto-confirm \
    --source-worktree-type psp-p2p \
    --psp-landing-worktree {LANDING_WORKTREE} \
    --psp-p2p-worktree {P2P_WORKTREE} \
    --ppp-worktree push-parser-panel"
```

**⚠️ CRITICAL**: Triad parameters are **MANDATORY** for resetup mode. Use `--auto-confirm` only for automated testing.

**Non-Destructive Rebuild (Preserves Database)**:
```bash
# Option 1: Full rebuild (DEFAULT) - composer + npm + build + caches
cd /home/lkonga/codes/psp-p2p
./scripts/local-sudo-runner/sudo-runner.sh --trunner \
  "./scripts/setup-worktree.sh {WORKTREE_NAME} \
    --rebuild-full \
    --source-worktree-type psp-p2p \
    --psp-landing-worktree {LANDING_WORKTREE} \
    --psp-p2p-worktree {P2P_WORKTREE} \
    --ppp-worktree push-parser-panel"

# Option 2: Frontend only - npm run build + view:clear (Fastest)
./scripts/local-sudo-runner/sudo-runner.sh --trunner \
  "./scripts/setup-worktree.sh {WORKTREE_NAME} \
    --rebuild-frontend \
    --source-worktree-type psp-p2p \
    --psp-landing-worktree {LANDING_WORKTREE} \
    --psp-p2p-worktree {P2P_WORKTREE} \
    --ppp-worktree push-parser-panel"

# Option 3: Backend only - composer install + cache clear
./scripts/local-sudo-runner/sudo-runner.sh --trunner \
  "./scripts/setup-worktree.sh {WORKTREE_NAME} \
    --rebuild-backend \
    --source-worktree-type psp-p2p \
    --psp-landing-worktree {LANDING_WORKTREE} \
    --psp-p2p-worktree {P2P_WORKTREE} \
    --ppp-worktree push-parser-panel"

# Option 4: Database only - migrate + config:clear
./scripts/local-sudo-runner/sudo-runner.sh --trunner \
  "./scripts/setup-worktree.sh {WORKTREE_NAME} \
    --rebuild-migrate \
    --source-worktree-type psp-p2p \
    --psp-landing-worktree {LANDING_WORKTREE} \
    --psp-p2p-worktree {P2P_WORKTREE} \
    --ppp-worktree push-parser-panel"

# Option 5: Test-gated rebuild (add --include-tests to any rebuild mode)
./scripts/local-sudo-runner/sudo-runner.sh --trunner \
  "./scripts/setup-worktree.sh {WORKTREE_NAME} \
    --rebuild-full \
    --include-tests \
    --source-worktree-type psp-p2p \
    --psp-landing-worktree {LANDING_WORKTREE} \
    --psp-p2p-worktree {P2P_WORKTREE} \
    --ppp-worktree push-parser-panel"
```

**⚠️ CRITICAL**: Triad parameters (`--psp-landing-worktree`, `--psp-p2p-worktree`, `--ppp-worktree`) are **MANDATORY** for all rebuild modes. They are required for triad rewiring verification.

**Note**: `--include-tests` flag runs test suite after rebuild; aborts on failure (test-gated).

**⚠️ CRITICAL**: Triad parameters (`--psp-landing-worktree`, `--psp-p2p-worktree`, `--ppp-worktree`) are **MANDATORY** for all rebuild modes. They are required for triad rewiring verification.

**Note**: Other params like `--source-branch` and `--setup-laravel` are **automatically ignored** with warnings in rebuild modes.

See **`references/worktree-update-rebuild.md`** for detailed rebuild scenarios.

